{"title":"Jiggle Cat","link":"https://kottke.org/25/12/jiggle-cat","date":1765233744000,"content":"\n        <p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/images/posts/01/img-47981-01.png\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/images/posts/01/img-47981-01.png 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/images/posts/01/img-47981-01.png 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1344\" height=\"1538\" alt=\"optical illusion of a black cat that jiggles when you shake your phone\" /></p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/What/comments/1pdp33i/what_is_the_science_behind_this/\">This is a pretty good optical illusion</a>. If you’re not on your phone, it also works if you shake your head a little. (thx, caroline)</p>\n\n        \n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/optical%20illusions\">optical illusions</a></p>\n\n         <p>💬 <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/12/jiggle-cat\">Join the discussion on kottke.org</a> →</p>\n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"0ec422d208217708e3b03239ae03fa4adba3df87cb63b5944e849fa19a877381","category":"Sites"}